# <PROJECT_NAME> Android — Global Directive

When working on `<REPO_FOLDER>` / `<APPLICATION_ID>`, you MUST read and strictly follow ALL rules in `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`. That file wins over this one.

MANDATORY:

1. Answer in chat first. Plans use native `implementation_plan.md` artifacts (`RequestFeedback: true`) with the interactive Proceed button — do NOT use `ask_question` for plan approval. Clicking Proceed (or confirming in chat) constitutes developer approval, triggering `workflow.py approve --source conversation` and `workflow.py begin`. When other developer decisions, sign-offs, or clarifications are required (engineering tradeoffs, policy/budget escalation, sensitive delivery, review round cap, device sign-off, or material ambiguity), universally prompt the developer using the interactive `ask_question` tool with clear, structured choices in the developer's conversation language. Reviewers run automatically without approval. Never demand terminal execution for approvals. Never put `(Recommended)` on Pass/Fail.
2. Delivery gate: reviewers run automatically upon completing implementation. Immediately and automatically launch exactly one `invoke_subagent` with all five leaves — `bug-reviewer-agent`, `convention-reviewer-agent`, `security-reviewer-agent`, `perf-anr-guardian-agent`, `regression-impact-reviewer-agent` — and the same `HARNESS_REVIEW_PACKAGE` path printed by `review_package.py` (rename the env token if you rebrand). NEVER pause to ask or wait for developer approval to launch reviewers. Wait for `*_PASS`. Record verdicts with `python .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --reviewer <name> --verdict PASS --evidence-pkg <sha12>` (or `--verdict <name>=PASS`). Do not invoke `code-review-guard-agent`. Do not wait for `LGTM`.
3. Quality over tokens. Never skip or serialize those five leaves to save resources.
4. Follow this checkout’s device policy from setup (physical only, emulator allowed, or either if they skipped). Resolve serial from `adb devices`. Never hardcode a serial.
5. Git policy: follow `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` for this checkout (do not assume the source project's "never commit" rule).
6. Zero chat clutter. Never echo raw `<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>` or Gradle dumps.
7. Discovery & execution efficiency: Discovery MUST start with `python .agents/scripts/project_graph.py --feature <name>` or `--find <Symbol>`; unanchored grep cascades are forbidden. Never poll or loop on `manage_task status` during background tasks; wait for reactive notifications. When code fixes are needed during verification, run `python .agents/scripts/workflow.py resume` to return to `IMPLEMENTING`.

Every rule in `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` is mandatory.
